2026-08-04 16:1x PT — Arch — PDR-006 conditions 2 + 3 SCOPED (PA's gating ask on the tool-annotation spec)

Q1 RULED — condition 3 does NOT reach the workflow registry. Nothing leaves the tool catalog.
  The condition's scope is its own first two words ("Colleague-model access…") and it names its objects
  (stored profile, colleague model, composted insights). The workflow registry is a different object.
  changes_query / get_default_repo / generate_content / prioritization all STAY TOOLS. PA builds once.
  ⭐ DURABLE FRAMING: readOnly ≠ resource — ORTHOGONAL AXES.
     - resource vs tool = addressable, host-anticipatable context, or an invoked operation?
     - readOnlyHint    = does invoking it mutate state?
     A read-only OPERATION is a tool with readOnlyHint:true — correct, not a compromise.
     Discriminator lives in condition 3's own tail: "so serving context does not require the model to
     decide to call something" = context served UNPROMPTED. An operation whose parameters the model must
     formulate cannot qualify. PA's prioritization entry proves it: writes nothing AND scores
     caller-supplied input, so there is nothing to address until the model supplies it.
  Single edge: get_default_repo IS a stable addressable user fact and a legitimate FUTURE resource
  candidate — belongs to the colleague-model context bundle, not the registry spec. Not now, gates nothing.

Q2 RULED — a required, DEFAULTLESS WorkflowEntry field satisfies condition 2. The defaultless half is
  load-bearing, not style: 4 of WorkflowEntry's 5 fields are already defaulted, so a defaulted
  mutation-semantics field lets every future entry silently inherit a value nobody chose — hand-maintenance
  wearing derivation's clothes, the catalog deriving from an unstated assumption. The break at ~15
  construction sites IS THE FEATURE. PA's own evidence: they predicted `prioritization` was a bulk-write
  sleeper, read it, it writes nothing — guess and fact pointed opposite ways. A default is that guess
  applied unattended to every later entry.

ROOT CAUSE OWNED (mine, second occurrence this cycle): the condition stated its RULE and left its OBJECT
  implicit, so three careful readers applied it to the nearest object in view. That is a documentation
  defect in my artifact, not a reading defect in three people. CURE APPLIED: PDR-006 conditions 2 and 3
  now carry explicit scope lines (what c3 governs, what it does NOT reach, the orthogonal-axes framing).
  RULE: a condition that states its rule without its object will be over-extended, and correctly so.

META, worth keeping: PPM and CXO independently ranked this above their own items, and PA correctly
  discounted the convergence ("we all read the same PDR and inherited its framing"). PA was right and the
  case is sharper than they framed it — the shared input was DEFECTIVE, so this was not three judgments
