2026-08-29 ~12:1x PT [exec, recording PM's standing directive on the attention rollup] 🔴 THE ROLLUP IS THE FLAG, AND AGE IS AN ESCALATION SIGNAL. PM verbatim: *"I'd say for something to be truly flagged for my attention, it needs to be included in your roll-up. If not addressed and sitting around for more than a day or so, it needs to be escalated as something that is perhaps being overlooked and may need my attention more urgently than it seems."* TWO SEPARATE REQUIREMENTS, both now in `.claude/skills/cohort-attention-rollup/SKILL.md` as Step 2b. **(a) Nothing counts as "flagged for PM" unless it is on the board.** A memo saying "flagging to PM," a commit message saying "flagging for confirmation," a 🟡 in a carry-forward — none of these are flagging. EARNED THE SAME DAY: the Apache 2.0 adoption commit `a4547d7c4` (2026-08-13) set the copyright holder to "Piper Morgan" and said explicitly *"flagging to PM for confirmation, not asserting it as settled"* — **it sat 16 days**, was never on any board because it lived in a commit message, and PM ruled on it in seconds once surfaced. The delay was the routing's, never PM's. Consequence for the skill: Step 1's source set (carry-forwards + GitHub + blocker mail) is a FLOOR, not a ceiling — it structurally catches only items whose authors knew to route them, and misses anything flagged in passing inside a commit body, issue comment, doc status line, or memo closing paragraph. **(b) Every decision item carries a FIRST-SEEN date; >~1 day unaddressed escalates.** ⭐ THE REASONING MATTERS MORE THAN THE THRESHOLD, and it inverts the natural read: an item sitting untouched usually does NOT mean PM deprioritized it — far more often **PM never understood what was being asked**, because the board's one-line framing under-described it. Two same-day proofs: the docs-tree flattening plan waited **18 days** and PM ruled instantly on learning it was a yes/no about ONE directory (*"Ah yes, the doc-tree! I requested this."*); and PM had to come back and ask what six separate board items actually WERE, because the board carried the asks and not the substance. **So age is a signal about the BOARD's framing, not about PM's priorities — when an item ages, re-describe it before re-listing it.** ★ AND THE SYMMETRY WORTH KEEPING: this is PM's own trigger ruling from the same morning applied to Exec's own instrument. **A board entry with no aging mechanism is a document with no trigger** — it renders, it is correct, and nothing fires. It just sits, which is exactly what 16 days and 18 days look like. The rule that governs the corpus governs the board that watches the corpus. — Exec
